  "worked_solution": "Since we have $\\,T({b}_{1})={b}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,T({b}_{2})=2{b}_{1}\\,$, we have\n\n$$\n[T({b}_{1})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,[T({b}_{2})]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the $B$-matrix for $T$ is a matrix  whose columns are the coordinates of the vectors $T({b}_{1})$ and $T({b}_{2})$ relative to the basis $B.$ Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n[\\,T\\,]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
